status: 404

NOT PROBED, and not probeable. mmtf.rcsb.org is retired: it has no DNS record
at all (getent hosts -> nothing, curl -> "Could not resolve host"). Every
marker under svc/ records a status read off the live service. This one cannot,
and says so here rather than leaving a reader to infer it from a missing date
-- a marker nobody finished writing and a marker that cannot be written look
identical otherwise.

What it declares instead is this mirror's own contract for the route. The
corpus is the 82 entries under blobs/v1.0/{full,reduced}/ and nothing else
exists; ZZZZ is not one of them, so a request for it names no structure, and
404 is the status that says so. 404 is also what the client code is written
against -- MmtfReader's downloader treats any non-200 as a failed fetch and
never branches on which non-200 it was. What matters is that the answer is
written down rather than arrived at by falling off the end of the route.

Why ZZZZ and not a rule for every id outside the corpus: a route that answered
every unknown id with a polite 404 would make a mistyped real id -- a fixture
somebody meant to write and did not -- indistinguishable from a deliberate one.
Absence stays loud by default, and is declared one id at a time.

This file is /v1.0/full/ZZZZ. Its twin under the other directory says the same
thing about the other half of the route; both exist because MmtfReader has a
downloader for each.

ZZZZ is a safe choice of non-entry: the PDB has issued no id beginning with Z
in this format, and the four-character alnum shape still passes the route's own
id validation, so the request reaches the corpus check rather than being
rejected one step earlier as malformed.
